(4790987, 691036, 76430, '<td valign="top">I figured out what this was right away looking at it again now.  Yes, you''re right, a rear-curtain flash would really help.  However rather than taking 100 shots or maybe 1000 if you''re trying to get the exact timing of the rear flash you could fake it like others have and have the ball stationary on the line at the start of a long exposure and jerk it away with monofilament.</td>', 'I figured out what this was right away looking at it again now.  Yes, you''re right, a rear-curtain flash would really help.  However rather than taking 100 shots or maybe 1000 if you''re trying to get the exact timing of the rear flash you could fake it like others have and have the ball stationary on the line at the start of a long exposure and jerk it away with monofilament.', '2008-06-30 03:05:29.000000', NULL, 0),
