(4794824, 690693, 21124, '<td valign="top">So I was wrong, it''s not a mirror lens. I''m very surprised to see a kit lens producing this kind of bokeh.<br/>By looking at your other pictures, I noticed that you have a somehow similar bokeh there, but with a different lens:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=669633" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/847/120/669633.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/847/120/669633.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/847/120/669633.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I am now wondering if this could be YOU doing something "unusual" instead of the lenses...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-01 14:06:57.</i></td>', 'So I was wrong, it''s not a mirror lens. I''m very surprised to see a kit lens producing this kind of bokeh.By looking at your other pictures, I noticed that you have a somehow similar bokeh there, but with a different lens:  I am now wondering if this could be YOU doing something "unusual" instead of the lenses...', '2008-07-01 15:01:44.000000', '2008-07-01 15:06:57.000000', 0),
(4795133, 690936, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>There are a lot of things right with this shot; things that i like.  I like the symmetry of it, the motion implied by the balls in different positions and the coloring of it. <br/> <br/>It feels a bit tight, left to right, as far as the crop goes, though.  At least to me.  If there were a way to make it just a shade wider without getting too many distracting elements, it might help.<br/> <br/>I do think it meets the challenge, so you did well there.  On the monitor I''m using right now, it feels a tad dark, but I don''t remember it being like that when I looked at it initially, earlier, so it "might" be a bit dark, and it may not be. :)<br/> <br/>Interesting shot.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat There are a lot of things right with this shot; things that i like.  I like the symmetry of it, the motion implied by the balls in different positions and the coloring of it.  It feels a bit tight, left to right, as far as the crop goes, though.  At least to me.  If there were a way to make it just a shade wider without getting too many distracting elements, it might help. I do think it meets the challenge, so you did well there.  On the monitor I''m using right now, it feels a tad dark, but I don''t remember it being like that when I looked at it initially, earlier, so it "might" be a bit dark, and it may not be. :) Interesting shot. Karma', '2008-07-01 16:35:12.000000', NULL, 0),
