(4800236, 691113, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color Saturationa and Hue:  Colors and saturation are very nice.  Hues are believeable.<br/> <br/>Brightness and contrast are good.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field are very good.<br/> <br/>I think the problem here is you have this really nice sunset(?) photo, with light poles in the way.  The rays of light grabb the eye and pull it down to the lower left corner, all the while fighting the light poles.  End result two subjects, one picture. <br/> <br/>The light poles sort of pop out of nowhere, and look a bit tilted.  The litteralists also probably voted you down a bit because there were two light poles rather than one.  (Oh yes, it does happen.)<br/> <br/>As this is an advanced edtiting challenge, I would like to see this picture done without the light poles, and then one of the sun''s rays highlited for that single line.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color Saturationa and Hue:  Colors and saturation are very nice.  Hues are believeable. Brightness and contrast are good. Focus and depth of field are very good. I think the problem here is you have this really nice sunset(?) photo, with light poles in the way.  The rays of light grabb the eye and pull it down to the lower left corner, all the while fighting the light poles.  End result two subjects, one picture.  The light poles sort of pop out of nowhere, and look a bit tilted.  The litteralists also probably voted you down a bit because there were two light poles rather than one.  (Oh yes, it does happen.) As this is an advanced edtiting challenge, I would like to see this picture done without the light poles, and then one of the sun''s rays highlited for that single line.', '2008-07-02 23:58:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4800264, 691108, 13759, '<td valign="top">I noticed this picture with a great DOF usage. The blured background altought seems to be PSed. But I really noticed an error in your material description. You put Canon 18-55 f3.5-56 as your lens and the apperture like f2.8. But... Given the astonishing backgound I really concern about this is a real apperture you had used. What was the correct lens used?</td>', 'I noticed this picture with a great DOF usage. The blured background altought seems to be PSed. But I really noticed an error in your material description. You put Canon 18-55 f3.5-56 as your lens and the apperture like f2.8. But... Given the astonishing backgound I really concern about this is a real apperture you had used. What was the correct lens used?', '2008-07-03 00:23:51.000000', NULL, 0),
